    "goal": "Size the PLINK binary .bed dataset and per-chromosome files for a GWAS cohort of 9148 samples and 2623973 variants (1214300 on the largest chromosome).",
    "rationale": "PLINK binary .bed packs 2 bits per sample per variant. The full-dataset .bed size is computed from n_samples × n_variants; the per-chromosome .bed size uses the largest chromosome's variant count. The number of per-chromosome files equals the number of chromosomes in the human reference build (25: 22 autosomes + X + Y + MT), a standard biological convention for a human GWAS split with --chr.",
